cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use figtracer, please cite it as below."
title: "figtracer: provenance from analysis notebook chunks to the figures and tables in lab notes"
abstract: >-
  A command-line toolkit that keeps the figures and tables in Markdown lab notes in step
  with the R and Python notebook chunks that produced them. Each saved figure or table is
  recorded with its notebook, chunk and git commit in a manifest; labelled Quarto chunks can
  be re-run headlessly; and numbers written in a note are checked against the saved outputs.
  It does not depend on a particular analysis or plotting library.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "David G."
    family-names: Priest
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0095-6718"
    affiliation: "Wing Lab, Center for Infectious Disease Education and Research (CIDER), Osaka University, Japan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/david-priest/figtracer"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21288979"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.1
date-released: 2026-11-03
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - provenance
  - electronic lab notebook
  - scientific workflow
  - single-cell
  - cytometry
